[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High Level System Architecture

Main Modules

The design of the application is based on the MVVM pattern. There are three core components in the MVVM pattern: the model, the view, and the view model. Each serves a distinct purpose. The diagram below shows the relationships between the three components.

The MVVN design pattern is implemented in the application as follows: the 4 th layer is the gRPC wrapper for communication with database services.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H10SG-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-11
TITLE: Data management API
STATEMENT: >>>
In embedded database mode, the indoor application hosts a local gRPC database API backed by an encrypted SQLite database. The existing unary API operations store and retrieve data, and streaming subscriptions deliver change notifications. The listener can serve other gRPC clients; database persistence does not require a remote or centralized database service. Existing non-embedded configurations retain their configured database service.

The list of API functions is defined in the following protocol document:

GBSK DB API
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-55
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-12
TITLE: Patients' Data Management
STATEMENT: >>>
In embedded database mode, the indoor application stores and manages patient information, treatment plans, and treatment history in its local relational repository. SQLCipher protects the whole database, including all patient and non-patient tables, rather than encrypting only patient demographic fields.

The data shall be managed in a relational database, which shall support hierarchical organization based on user flow.

The data shall be stored in the form of JSON-serialized Protocol Buffers based on the communication protocol.
Each Protocol Buffers structure shall have a dedicated database table with the following fields:

- ``id``: integer primary key with AUTOINCREMENT, retained in the serialized entity.
- ``parent_id``: non-null integer, present for child-entity tables to retain the parent-child hierarchy; not present in every table.
- ``data``: non-null TEXT containing the serialized Protocol Buffers JSON.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-55
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-377
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-13
TITLE: High Level System Architecture
STATEMENT: >>>
Approvals Calibration - Heater current configuration.

The application is comprised of two key components: GBSK Device Control console (Indoor application) and Treatment Control console (Outdoor application).

The GBSK Device Control console is integrated within the GBSK device. This application addresses functionalities related to patients, demographic data management, clinical data management, treatment data management, user access, clinical workflows, and system setup and services.

The Treatment Control application must be located in a console outside the treatment room. This is to provide the operator with a safe work environment. It should allow healthcare professionals e.g., radiation therapists (RTT), and physicians to activate the radiation emission for the patient's treatment and to provide tools for physicists to program the system's calibration values.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-54
  ROLE: Refines

