[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-625
TITLE: Approve Patient's Treatment Fields (Plan)
STATEMENT: >>>
Sequence diagram for 'approve plan' use case:

Approval credential validation honors the persisted account lockout threshold but neither increments nor resets failed-login attempts. Rejected approval credentials leave the plan unchanged.

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    
    box rgb(245, 245, 245) Application
        participant PlanViewModel
        participant PlanModel
    end
    
    box rgb(245, 245, 245) Server
        participant Storage
    end

    User->>PlanViewModel: change plan status
    PlanViewModel->>User: show dialog
    User->>PlanViewModel: credentials & desired status
    
    PlanViewModel->>Storage: authenticate user
    activate Storage
    Storage->>Storage: handle request
    Storage-->>PlanViewModel: response
    deactivate Storage
    
    alt successful authentication
        PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: change plan status
        
        PlanModel->>Storage: save changes
        activate Storage
        Storage->>Storage: save plan
        Storage-->>PlanModel: saved plan
        deactivate Storage
    end
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-17
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-626
TITLE: Refresh Patient's Treatment Fields from the database
STATEMENT: >>>

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User

       box Application
           participant PlanViewModel
           participant PlanModel
       end

       box Server
           participant Storage
       end

       User->>PlanViewModel: refresh treatment fields
       activate PlanViewModel
       PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: fetch fields
       activate PlanModel
       
       Note over PlanModel: clear displayed fields
       PlanModel->>Storage: query stored fields
       activate Storage
       Note over Storage: handle request
       Storage-->>PlanModel: treatment fields
       deactivate Storage
       
       Note over PlanModel: update displayed fields
       PlanModel-->>PlanViewModel: 
       PlanViewModel-->>User: display fields

       PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: validate field doses
       Note over PlanModel: verify dose calculations
       PlanModel-->>PlanViewModel: validity status
       deactivate PlanModel

       alt validation fails
           Note over PlanViewModel: disable treatment
           PlanViewModel-->>User: show warning
       end
       deactivate PlanViewModel
   </pre>

Fulfilled requirements:
- RQ-H10SG-18-#9: Patients - Plan view - Refresh Patient's Treatment Fields from the database
- RQ-H10SG-21-#11: Patients - Plan view - View Patient's Plan's Treatment Fields
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-162
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-628
TITLE: Update Patient's Treatment Fields for a Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
Update patient's treatment fields:
1. If the plan is not approved, a read-only plan is displayed.
2. Otherwise, emission duration input is enabled.
3. User selects fields.
4. If a single field is selected, the delete button is enabled.
5. Otherwise, the add button or update and delete buttons are enabled depending on if it is an existing plan field.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-192
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-629
TITLE: Search Filtering
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide search and filtering capabilities in the system logs view to allow operators to find and view specific log entries. The search and filtering functionality shall enable filtering by various criteria to help locate relevant system events.

The sequence diagram for the search filtering process is provided in the attached diagram.

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User

       box Application
           participant LogViewModel
           participant CreateFilterDialog
       end

       alt adding a filter
           User->>LogViewModel: add filter
           activate LogViewModel
           LogViewModel->>CreateFilterDialog: show dialog
           activate CreateFilterDialog
           CreateFilterDialog-->>User: select field to filter
           User->>CreateFilterDialog: selected field
           CreateFilterDialog-->>User: select message type
           User->>CreateFilterDialog: selected type
           CreateFilterDialog-->>LogViewModel: 
           deactivate CreateFilterDialog
           
           Note over LogViewModel: add new filter
           LogViewModel-->>User: updated list of records
           deactivate LogViewModel
       end

       alt removing a filter
           User->>LogViewModel: remove chosen filter
           activate LogViewModel
           Note over LogViewModel: remove the filter
           LogViewModel-->>User: updated list of records
           deactivate LogViewModel
       end
   </pre>

Fulfilled requirements:
- RQ-H10SG-22-#9: System Logs' View - Search Filtering

Attachments:
- H10SG-22.sequence.mermaid.drawio.png (121.61 kB)
<<<
