[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-676
TITLE: Register and Update Collimator Flow
STATEMENT: >>>
1. Identify the connected collimator.

2. Open the New Collimator form with the serial of the identified collimator, or open the Edit Collimator form for a registered collimator.

3. When the user saves the form, the target-management view model passes the selected Active value to the collimator service. The service passes that value to the repository when creating a collimator and copies it to the updated collimator when editing one, so the repository persists the selected value in the Collimator table's ``IsActive`` field.

Before the collimator model is populated, the service fetches the active Head record. If none is active, the repository reactivates the existing Head with serial ``00000`` or, when that record does not exist, creates it as active with the current creation date. The resulting active Head is used as the foreign-key parent when a new collimator is saved. Head persistence requests include the creation date.
<<<
