[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-680
TITLE: New Collimator Mandatory Fields
STATEMENT: >>>
The Mandatory field of a Collimator should be:

- Serial - Automatically identified from telemetry.

- Type, Energy, and SSD should be fetched/saved from the Configuration Table.

Collimator Table

+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| Name                       | Type    | constraint | Description                                   |
+============================+=========+============+===============================================+
| ID                         | Int64   | Not Null   | Primary key. Auto incremental                 |
+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| HeadID                     | Int64   | Not Null   | Foreign Key to Head table                     |
+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| CollimatorConfigurati onID | Int64   | Not Null   | Foreign Key to CollimatorConfigurati on table |
+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| CreateDate                 | Date    | Not Null   |                                               |
+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| Serial                     | String  | Not Null   | Unique                                        |
+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| IsActive                   | Tinyint | Not Null   |                                               |
+----------------------------+---------+------------+-----------------------------------------------+

CollimatorConfiguration Table

+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+
| Name               | Type           | constraint | Description                                                    |
+====================+================+============+================================================================+
| ID                 | Int64          |            |                                                                |
+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+
| CreateDate         | DateTime       | Not Null   |                                                                |
+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+
| Type               | TargetTypeEnum | Not Null   | Unique with Energy and SSD                                     |
+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+
| Energy             | Energy Enum    | Not Null   | Unique with Type and SSD                                       |
+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+
| SSD                | SSDType Enum   | Not Null   | Unique with Type and Energy                                    |
+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+
| ReferencedDoseRate | Decimal        |            | Dose rate in the a specific cell in the collimator that serves |
+--------------------+----------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+


<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-321
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-681
TITLE: Device ID Validation Flow
STATEMENT: >>>
The Device ID is mandatory for the application to be able to run. The application should validate the existence of the DeviceID on startup.

If no Device ID is present in settings, the user asked to enter such ID in a pop-up modal. The ID is saved to settings and presisted to the database.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-249
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-682
TITLE: Emission Current Calculation
STATEMENT: >>>
The Current should be auto-calculated as the quotient of Power[W] divided by Energy Level[kV]:

Emission Current[mA] = Power[W] / Voltage[kV]

The device shall operate at a constant power of 50W.

Here are the calculated values as a dependency on Energy Level:

+----------+-------------+----------------------+
| Power[W] | Voltage[kV] | Emission Current[mA] |
+==========+=============+======================+
| 50       | 50          | 1                    |
+----------+-------------+----------------------+
| 50       | 70          | 0.71                 |
+----------+-------------+----------------------+
| 50       | 100         | 0.5                  |
+----------+-------------+----------------------+
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-232
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-683
TITLE: Calculate Emission Duration
STATEMENT: >>>
The Field Actual Dose should be auto-calculate from the duration using the following function:

[Field Output factor] * [Dose Rate cGy/min] * Duration / 60

i.e. 1.05 * 320 * 18 / 60 = 100.8 cGy

Field Output factor - This value should be retrieved from the OutputFactor service.

Dose Rate - This value should be retrieved from the CollimatorConfiguration Service.

Duration - This value is calculated from the [PrescribedDose] / ([FieldOutputFactor] * [DoseRate]) * 60
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-231
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-739
  ROLE: Refines

