[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-686
TITLE: Lock application during active emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The application will be locked when a user loads a plan in the external application.
The application will use the Plan DB Event to determine when such a plan is loaded.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-187
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-687
TITLE: Load For Treatment Flow
STATEMENT: >>>
When a user loads a plan in the external application, the plan service persists the Pending plan and publishes it to both the ``PlanEvents`` and ``LoadForTreatmentEvents`` streams.

Each stream uses a broadcast event hub with an independent queue for every active subscriber. Publishing writes the same event to every subscriber instead of allowing subscribers to compete for one shared channel item. Stream cancellation removes that subscriber's queue.

The external application loads the plan from its load-for-treatment event. Every internal application subscribed to the plan event receives the same update and locks its plan screen.

For an incomplete treatment, the internal application prompts the user to choose the
remaining scalar emission or the complete scalar emission before publishing the selected
plan. The external application recalculates the scalar treatment time from the latest
treatment completion status.

The shared treatment-plan validation runs before a plan is accepted for load. It permits
one valid treatment field and rejects missing, additional, or invalid fields before the
firmware-session preparation path receives the plan.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-184
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-185
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-422
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-688
TITLE: Update Collimator Data Flow Diagram
STATEMENT: >>>
The application will send an update command to the Collimator Service. The following flow describes the flow:

1. User edits collimator.
2. Collimator form is opened.
3. Upon save, collimator configuration is persisted to the database using CollimatorCommands.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-128
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-689
TITLE: User Management and Reset Lockout
STATEMENT: >>>
1. The user requests to add a new user.
2. The user add form is cleared and enabled.
3. The form is validated. If validation fails, saving is disabled and the error is presented to the user.
4. The new user record is presisted to the database.

User Management displays the persisted failed-login count as lock status. Reset lockout is enabled only for a locked selection and an authenticated Administrator with an active, unlocked, unexpired session. The confirmed command calls ResetUserLockout with the target user ID through the user commands/repository transport, handles errors using the existing task/dialog flow, and refreshes the list after completion.

ResetUserLockout resolves the bearer token through the server's session registry, then reloads the actor and role from persisted storage. Only the exact built-in Administrator role on an existing, unlocked actor authorizes the operation; a supplied user ID or stale client role alone is not authority. Missing, forged, deleted, demoted, locked, and non-administrator actors are rejected.

For a target at or above 10 failed login attempts, one transaction sets only failed_login_attempts to zero and writes the reset-success security record with actor and target IDs. Failure to persist the audit rolls back the reset. The response contains the target user; a target below 10 is returned unchanged with no reset-success record. Password, last_accessed, and other user fields are preserved, and the client adds no duplicate success audit. Ordinary CRUD retains the output-only counter contract.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-68
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
