[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-705
TITLE: Save Patient Audit Log Records
STATEMENT: >>>
Sequence diagram for registering the current user and patient identifier once a requested patient change is successfully persisted. Failed, unchanged, reverted, or unapplied saves produce no successful-change audit. The record identifies the save operation, not demographic field values. Log persistence is queued and assigns the record timestamp.

Explicit navigation that displays a patient, diagnosis, simulation, prescription, or plan records the acting user and displayed record identifiers. Cached tab revisits and explicit returns to an already loaded record are views even without a database read; automatic navigation, background loads, and refreshes are not. A failed read is not recorded as a successful view of the unavailable record.

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
    box rgb(245, 245, 245) Application
        participant PatientsViewModel
        participant ActionAuditService
        participant DbLogRepository
        participant PatientEditing
        participant PatientListModel
        participant PatientRepository
    end

    box rgb(245, 245, 245) Server
        participant LogService
        participant PatientService
    end

    PatientsViewModel->>PatientEditing: SavePatientAsync()
    PatientEditing->>PatientListModel: SavePatientAsync(patient)
    alt [new patient]
        PatientListModel->>PatientRepository: CreateAsync(patient)
        PatientRepository->>PatientService: grpc:CreatePatient
        PatientService-->>PatientRepository: created patient
    else [existing patient]
        PatientListModel->>PatientRepository: UpdateAsync(old patient, new patient)
        PatientRepository->>PatientService: grpc:UpdatePatient
        PatientService-->>PatientRepository: updated patient
    end
    PatientRepository-->>PatientListModel: saved patient
    PatientListModel-->>PatientEditing: saved patient
    PatientEditing-->>PatientsViewModel: saved patient

    opt [requested change successfully persisted]
        PatientsViewModel->>ActionAuditService: RegisterAction(save completed with patient ID)
        ActionAuditService->>ActionAuditService: add current username and user ID
        ActionAuditService->>DbLogRepository: LogAsync(user audit record, not awaited)
        DbLogRepository->>LogService: CreateRecord
        LogService-->>DbLogRepository: persisted record with timestamp
    end
   </pre>
<<<
