  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-45
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-708
TITLE: Display System Telemetry
STATEMENT: >>>
The receive-only GCB telemetry service passes unsolicited device-information, telemetry,
and fault datagrams to the system telemetry processor. The operating mode in device
information selects the corresponding normal or calibration parser. The selected parser
translates the complete physical interlock status and required-interlock masks into
``SystemInterlocks`` while retaining both raw masks for service diagnostics. The calibration
parser validates the expanded 55-field payload while preserving fields 0 through 46. It
maps the appended collimator-ID low and high words at fields 47 and 48, Mag 1 X/Y/Z at
fields 49 through 51, and Mag 2 X/Y/Z at fields 52 through 54 into the same semantic
snapshot properties as the normal parser.

Valid immutable snapshots are published through the main-board model and GCB data store;
unsupported modes or malformed packets do not replace the last valid snapshot. Publication
is limited to one snapshot every
250 ms, and 1.5 seconds without valid telemetry produces an unavailable snapshot.
System readiness requires a clear buffered master-fault input, no active system fault,
and all required interlocks to be available and active.
<<<
